-\item D6 an unbounded discriminator generator loss;
-\item D7 strengths selected on 40-epoch inner models but reported on 80-epoch outer models;
-\item D8 a custom fastmath LISI;
-\item D9 one seed, overlapping folds as replicates, and 36 uncorrected tests of which 6 survive Holm.
-\end{itemize}
-\item Of the original paper's 25 substantive claims, 11 were invalidated by these defects, 6 never tested, 5 partially supported and 3 contradicted by its own data; no number of its Table 2, Figures 2--5 or Table S1 is reused \src{PAPER\_PLAN \S1; original\_manuscript\_claims\_audit.csv (project file outside the repository)}.
-\item The public preprint stays as it is and will be replaced by the next version with results \src{SI-07}.
 \item A code check of tag prereg-tier12-v1 led to fixes before tag prereg-tier12-v2 \src{SI-40; PREREG \S9, 2026-10-04}. A1 restarted from zero at tag prereg-tier12-v2; the 202 A1 fits made at prereg-tier12-v1 stay on disk, unused, and no A1 metric value from them informed any decision \src{SI-43}.
 \item The strength ranges of X1 come from 3 of the 8 tasks (atac\_small, immune, sim1), fitted on seeds 100--102, disjoint from X1; no A1 fit is used as an X1 fit \src{PREREG, Disclosure (for Methods); SI-13}.
 \item Strength-grid edges: X1 tasks whose matched strength falls on a grid edge are extended by rule R4 for matching only, and edge optima are disclosed per task \src{PREREG \S8; SI-55}.
